    "title": "Minimal chain stitch",
    "author": "Basti Tee",
    "description": "An example of a minimal chain stitch. You start from the inside at the leftmost station, then into the middle hole and continuing on the inside to the right hole. From there you chain-stitch around the thread at the middle hole back into the right hole and then finish the thread on the inside."
